# DAST authorization scope.
#
# guard_scope.sh reads this file and blocks any active-scan command whose
# target is not listed here. One entry per line; blank lines and lines
# starting with # are ignored.
#
# Accepted entry forms:
#   127.0.0.1          exact IPv4 literal
#   localhost          exact hostname
#   app.example.test   exact hostname
#
# Matching is exact and case-insensitive on the host portion only. A URL
# target such as http://localhost:8080/login matches the entry "localhost".
# There is no wildcard support: a wildcard in an authorization boundary is
# how out-of-scope hosts get scanned by accident.
#
# Only add a host you can demonstrate you are authorised to test. Active
# scanning of third-party infrastructure is unlawful in most jurisdictions.
# The agent is instructed never to edit this file — a human must.

localhost
127.0.0.1
::1
